$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: usm/docs-experience
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-08-14"
summary: >-
  Overhaul the generated docs site from a spec-dump into a real reading experience — suppress empty
  templated stubs, surface the real TOGAF deliverables in the nav, widen the layout to use the
  viewport, rebuild the homepage as navigation, and give the help and technical audiences distinct
  voices.
$system: usm/system
$service: usm/cli
intent: >-
  Strategic review found the docs generators faithfully dump .usm content into VitePress defaults
  but do not author a reading experience. Around 30 of 127 pages are empty placeholder stubs
  (including a UI map for a CLI); the real TOGAF detailed-design output exists but is orphaned from
  the nav; content is squeezed into VitePress's 688px default; the homepage is a layout:home hero
  with no sidebar plus a README-style metrics dump; and the help/technical audiences differ only by
  filtering, never by voice. Because usm generate produces this for every consumer
  (daingerdainger-com and others), every flaw ships to every downstream docs site.
status: built
flows:
  - id: suppress-stubs
    name: Suppress templated stubs a service has no data for
    description: >-
      A service only emits the architecture/ui/deployment/operations/decisions pages its .usm
      actually populates. A CLI gets no UI map or production-deployment page.
    steps:
      - action: inspect
        id: s1
        target: each templated page generator checks whether the source service carries that section data
      - action: omit
        id: s2
        target: skip emitting the page when the section is empty rather than writing a placeholder
      - action: prune
        id: s3
        target: the matching sidebar entry is also omitted so nav has no dead links
  - id: surface-togaf
    name: Surface the real TOGAF deliverables as the Architecture section
    description: >-
      The togaf generator already produces Phase A-H deliverables; wire them into the dev-docs
      sidebar as a real Architecture section instead of empty per-service architecture stubs.
    steps:
      - action: generate
        id: s1
        target: togaf output into the docs tree (not a parallel orphaned directory)
      - action: wire
        id: s2
        target: >-
          sidebar Architecture group with Vision, Business, Data, Application, Technology,
          Governance links
      - action: scope
        id: s3
        target: help audience omits the Architecture section (internal detail)
  - id: widen-layout
    name: Widen the layout to use the viewport
    description: Override VitePress defaults so reference content, tables, code, and diagrams breathe.
    steps:
      - action: set
        id: s1
        target: "--vp-layout-max-width and content-container max-width via generated theme CSS"
      - action: enable
        id: s2
        target: full-width code blocks and tables that break out of the prose column
  - id: rebuild-homepage
    name: Rebuild the homepage as navigation
    description: >-
      Drop the README-style metrics/identity dump; keep the hero and add a features grid whose cards
      ARE the navigation into the docs.
    steps:
      - action: drop
        id: s1
        target: the At-a-glance, Identity, Who-its-for, Next-steps body markdown from index.md
      - action: add
        id: s2
        target: >-
          a features grid of cards linking to Getting Started, Schema, CLI, MCP, Architecture (dev
          only)
      - action: keep
        id: s3
        target: the hero actions (Get Started, Schema Reference)
  - id: audience-voice
    name: Give help and technical audiences distinct voices
    description: >-
      The same feature spec renders differently per audience — task-oriented for help,
      reference-faithful for technical.
    steps:
      - action: render
        id: s1
        target: >-
          help voice leads with when-to-run, example output, troubleshooting, derived from flows and
          contracts
      - action: render
        id: s2
        target: >-
          technical voice is the full spec-faithful reference (intent, flows, contracts, tests,
          decisions)
      - action: share
        id: s3
        target: one source .usm file, two render paths
  - id: anti-drift
    name: Anti-drift and discoverability
    description: Pin the getting-started version from package.json and enable VitePress sitemap on both sites.
    steps:
      - action: derive
        id: s1
        target: getting-started install version from package.json, not a hardcoded string
      - action: enable
        id: s2
        target: sitemap.hostname in both VitePress configs
contracts:
  - id: no-empty-stubs
    description: No empty placeholder pages are emitted
    must_have:
      - A templated section page is emitted only when the source service carries data for it
      - Sidebar entries match emitted pages one-to-one (no dead links)
      - A CLI never gets ui, production-deployment, or observability pages
  - id: togaf-in-nav
    description: The real TOGAF deliverables are reachable from the technical docs nav
    must_have:
      - dev-docs sidebar has an Architecture group linking the Phase A-H deliverables
      - help audience omits the Architecture section
      - No parallel orphaned togaf directory
  - id: content-width
    description: Reference content uses the viewport, not VitePress's 688px default
    must_have:
      - "--vp-layout-max-width overridden to ~1280 or wider"
      - Code blocks and tables render full-width
      - Applies to every consumer site on their next generate
  - id: homepage-is-navigation
    description: The homepage is a navigation surface, not a metrics dump
    must_have:
      - No At-a-glance, Identity, or Who-its-for body markdown on index.md
      - A features grid of cards links into the primary doc sections
      - Hero actions retained
  - id: audience-voice-distinct
    description: Help and technical audiences read differently for the same feature
    must_have:
      - Help feature page leads with when-to-run and example output
      - Technical feature page is spec-faithful (full flows, contracts, tests)
      - Same source .usm, two render paths
  - id: no-handwritten-drift
    description: No hand-written drift in generated docs
    must_have:
      - getting-started install version derived from package.json
      - VitePress sitemap enabled on both audiences
decisions:
  - id: emit-only-when-populated
    decision: Emit a templated page only when its source section is populated; never write a placeholder
    rationale: >-
      A placeholder promises depth and delivers nothing — worse than the page not existing. Omission
      is honest.
  - id: togaf-as-architecture-section
    decision: Surface togaf output as the Architecture section of the docs site, not a separate target
    rationale: >-
      The detailed design already exists; the failure was discoverability. Wiring it into the nav
      fixes both the empty stubs and the orphaned output in one move.
  - id: css-not-config-for-width
    decision: Widen via generated theme CSS custom properties, not VitePress config knobs
    rationale: >-
      CSS custom properties are the documented override path and survive VitePress minor bumps;
      config knobs for layout do not exist.
  - id: feature-cards-as-nav
    decision: >-
      Use the VitePress features grid as homepage navigation rather than forcing a sidebar onto
      layout home
    rationale: >-
      Cards are the canonical landing-page nav pattern and keep the hero; forcing a sidebar means
      abandoning the home layout entirely.
  - id: voice-is-render-mode
    decision: Audience is a render mode (voice), not just a filter
    rationale: >-
      Filtering alone produced two identical sites; the brief needs two different documents from one
      source.
implementation:
  primary: src/generators/markdown.ts
  test_code: tests/generate.test.ts
  test_code_status: manual
see_also:
  - usm/gen-markdown
  - usm/gen-togaf
  - usm/cli-docs
